 "final_passage": "On the Tamsin-News test split, Verisum achieves a hallucination rate of 8.7%, compared with 11.0% for Corran-Sum with salience pre-filtering and 15.1% for Corran-Sum alone. The salience filter reduces the hallucination rate by 4.0 percentage points (from 15.1% to 11.0%), while Verisum's additional entity-grounding loss yields a further 2.3 percentage-point reduction (from 11.0% to 8.7%). The observed 27.2% relative reduction from salience pre-filtering is not directly comparable to the roughly 30% reduction attributed to this approach in prior work (Varga & Sandoval, 2021), as the cited passage does not specify the dataset or metric conditions for that figure. No statistical tests were reported, so these differences are descriptive only and should be interpreted with caution given the single training run per system.",
